# CountingMachine — Bowl with FIXED spiral inclined tracks (máng dốc)

## Track geometry reference

| Video | What we match |
|-------|----------------|
| [RNA Bowl Feeder for Spring](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ioa9o-LLHCA) | **Visible spiral inclined trough on bowl wall** (máng xoắn dốc) |
| [RNA EcoType](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/oszvi08exHI) | Orientation / single-file / wrong pose falls back |
| [Huibao rotary](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/jGgILsgO2yY) | Rotary disc drive (we do **not** use vibratory drive) |

RNA spring video = vibratory bowl. **This project uses rotary disc paddles** to push parts up the same style of **fixed spiral track**.

## Operating sequence

1. Bulk screws on rotating conical disc (paddles).
2. Parts enter **fixed helical trough (máng dốc)** climbing the bowl wall.
3. Elevated rim gate: correct pose → chute → slide → fall off tip.
4. Wrong pose falls inward off the track **back onto the disc**.

## SoT

- CAD: `3d_model/centrifugal_screw_feeder_cq.py` → fixed `spiral_track.stl`
- Sim: `3d_model/sim/screw_feeder_pybullet.py` (teal continuous track)
